cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MolSanity: a reliability audit for feature attributions on molecular graph neural networks"
message: "If you use this software or its released artifacts, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Karthik
    family-names: Iyer
    email: 22557016@students.latrobe.edu.au
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0593-1602"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Information Technology, La Trobe University, Melbourne, Victoria 3086, Australia"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kar488/molsanity"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - graph neural networks
  - explainability
  - feature attribution
  - molecular property prediction
  - scaffold shift
  - reliability
abstract: >-
  MolSanity audits existing feature-attribution methods for molecular graph
  neural networks rather than proposing a new one. It scores every
  (dataset, backbone, attributor, split) combination on six axes: motif-native
  coherence, occlusion-attribution faithfulness, ground-truth localisation
  where node labels exist, cross-checkpoint stability, calibration linkage, and
  confidence/correctness regime stratification. The released artifacts include
  trained checkpoints, per-molecule audit records, and the scripts that
  regenerate every figure and table of the accompanying manuscript.
